course: dictionary
lesson: 15767
title: Describing shape and size
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in just one word. «Tubby» is one of them. When you read that someone is tubby, you can see a short, round shape in your mind. Look for the clues around the word to check what it means.
explain: «The tubby little man laughed and rubbed his round belly.» The words round and belly are clues. They tell you tubby describes a short man who is rather fat with a round body.
explain: Tubby can also mean shaped like a tub: round and wide. «The tubby teapot sat on the table» is a teapot that is round and wide, not a teapot that is fat in the way a person is. Read the whole sentence to know which meaning fits.
explain: Tubby is informal. You will hear it in stories and in everyday talk, often in a friendly, joking way. Be careful when you use it about people, because it can hurt feelings if you say it unkindly.
fact: Tubby means short and rather fat, with a round body.
fact: Tubby can also mean shaped like a tub: round and wide.
fact: «Tubby» is informal, so you hear it more in stories and chatty talk than in formal writing.
fact: «A tubby cat» is a cat with a round, soft-looking body.
fact: Tubby, tubbier and tubbiest show how the word changes to compare: a tubbier cat is fatter than a tubby one, and the tubbiest is the fattest of all.
exercise: «The tubby cat sleeps all afternoon in the sun.» What does tubby mean? | Very fast and thin | *Short and round, a bit plump | Very tall and thin | Angry and loud
exercise: «The old tubby teapot sat on the shelf.» What shape does tubby suggest here? | *Round and wide, like a tub | Pointed like a tent | Long and thin like a pencil | Flat like a pancake
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as tubby? | Quick | Cold | Skinny | *Plump
test: «Grandad is getting a bit tubby, so he walks every day.» What does getting a bit tubby mean? | Getting lost on a walk | Getting a new job | Getting very tall | *Getting a little plumper
test: Why might a writer call a character tubby in a funny story? | To say the character is very far away | To say the character is very clever | To show the character is a robot | *To paint a friendly, round, soft-looking picture of them
exam: Which word from the choices means the same as tubby in «a tubby little man»? | Quiet | *Plump | Fast | Tall
